-- statement:
--   The first and fourth digits can be a digit from $2$ to $9$ ; there are $8$ such digits. The second, third, fifth, sixth, seventh, eighth, ninth, and tenth digits can be a digit from $0$ to $9$ ; there are $10$ such digits. Hence there are a total of $8^{2}\cdot 10^{8}= \boxed{ 6400000000 }$ Such phone numbers.
-- source:
